      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:69:3",
      "text": [
        " يَأْتِي يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ شَيْ‏ءٌ مِثْلُ الْكُبَّةِ فَيَدْفَعُ فِي ظَهْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِ فَيُدْخِلُهُ الْجَنَّةَ فَيُقَالُ هَذَا الْبِرُّ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Sayf, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘There would come, on the Day of Judgement, something like a globe, so it would push in the back of the Believer and enter him into the Paradise, and it would be said: ‘This is the righteousness’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Sayf from abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) who has said the following: “On the Day of Judgment something will suddenly come behind the believer, rush him forward and admit him in paradise. It will be said, ‘This is kindness.’” "
        ]
      }
